From 14d69afbb5a160a7e33e6daf0977b67b32321494 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: razgulay <bantran09@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:30:58 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(vertex): port the Vertex AI chat forwarding lane
 (fixes gemini-3.1-pro-preview 404)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The catalog shipped vertex/vertex-partner with models and dashboard
entries but no executor, so chat fell through to the generic OpenAI
forwarder which POSTed the registry BaseURL verbatim — bare
https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1 — and Google answered with its HTML
'404: The requested URL /v1 was not found on this server.' page for
every model, gemini-3.1-pro-preview included.

Port of open-sse/executors/vertex.js + translator/request/openai-to-vertex.js:
- vertex: Gemini-native generateContent / streamGenerateContent?alt=sse
  against publishers/google/models — project-scoped regional path for
  OAuth, global publishers endpoint + ?key= for express API keys.
- vertex-partner: OpenAI-compatible global openapi endpoint behind the
  project-scoped path, delegated to the generic forwarder with the final
  URL baked in.
- Auth: Service Account JSON (RS256 JWT assertion → Bearer, cached per
  client_email), ADC authorized_user JSON (refresh_token grant, cached
  per token), express raw key (?key=), or a pre-set accessToken.
- Body: TranslateOpenAIToGemini, then postProcessForVertex parity —
  thoughtSignature replaced with the Vertex-native default and
  functionCall/functionResponse ids stripped (Vertex rejects both).
- Registry BaseURL drops the /v1 suffix (host root, matching upstream).
